1
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,100
Okarin?

2
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:14,180
How?

3
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:17,890
How?

4
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:24,210
I can touch her. She's really here.

5
00:00:27,490 --> 00:00:29,130
You're not a ghost?

6
00:00:29,130 --> 00:00:31,620
Do you want me to call the cops?

7
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:33,640
I just want to know the truth!

8
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:35,640
You were stabbed here...

9
00:00:37,710 --> 00:00:39,080
What do you mean by "truth"?

10
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,870
Are you stupid? Do you want to die?

11
00:00:40,870 --> 00:00:42,740
That's Louise-chan's famous line!

12
00:00:42,740 --> 00:00:44,350
I saw it!

13
00:00:44,350 --> 00:00:45,970
You got stabbed!

14
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:48,520
Three hours ago,

15
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:50,360
at Doctor Nakabachi's press conference,
at the Radio Building!

16
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:52,980
Okarin, try to control your delusions.

17
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:55,760
Doctor Nakabachi's
press conference was called off!

18
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:56,890
But...

19
00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:59,720
Makise-san! It's almost time!

20
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:01,230
All right!

21
00:01:01,230 --> 00:01:03,060
Wait! Are you running away?

22
00:01:04,970 --> 00:01:06,430
You're...

23
00:01:06,430 --> 00:01:07,930
I have a name.

24
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:09,640
It's Hououin...

25
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:11,300
Kyouma!

26
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:49,140
Time Travel Paranoia

27
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:53,020
Are Time Machines Possible?

28
00:02:49,660 --> 00:02:53,020
Thank you all for coming here today.

29
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:59,060
I don't have much experience
with lectures like these.

30
00:02:59,060 --> 00:03:01,140
So I hope you'll bear with me.

31
00:03:01,140 --> 00:03:04,290
Makise Kurisu's giving the lecture...

32
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:07,460
So she isn't a ghost?

33
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:08,680
Still talking about that?

34
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:12,560
I've been asked to speak to you
about time machines.

35
00:03:13,070 --> 00:03:16,850
It's a different theme than that
of my <i>Science Magazine </i>essay,

36
00:03:16,850 --> 00:03:19,430
but I'd like to give it a try.

37
00:03:19,870 --> 00:03:21,060
Time machines?

38
00:03:21,060 --> 00:03:29,010
I believe that time machines are foolishness.

39
00:03:29,010 --> 00:03:32,820
I'd like to spend the lecture discussing
how I arrived at that conclusio—

40
00:03:32,820 --> 00:03:34,100
Objection!

41
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:38,140
Time machines are impossible?

42
00:03:38,140 --> 00:03:40,040
It's far too early to decide that!

43
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:42,140
Okarin, you're embarrassing yourself.

44
00:03:42,140 --> 00:03:43,410
You're...

45
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:52,140
I believe that "early" isn't the issue.

46
00:03:52,140 --> 00:03:54,600
It's theoretically impossible.

47
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:55,940
What?

48
00:03:57,270 --> 00:04:01,900
Well then, let's change the format
of this lecture to a discussion.

49
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:05,850
That will make it easier for
certain stubborn people to understand.

50
00:04:05,850 --> 00:04:09,030
Right? Hououin Kyouma-san?

51
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:22,980
Makise Kurisu...

52
00:04:22,980 --> 00:04:24,550
And from this,

53
00:04:24,550 --> 00:04:26,900
we can conclude that,
in a string theory-based universe,

54
00:04:26,900 --> 00:04:28,870
time travel is unrealistic.

55
00:04:28,870 --> 00:04:30,420
You want to try it?

56
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:32,600
Hououin-san?

57
00:04:34,180 --> 00:04:35,860
I imagine so...

58
00:04:35,860 --> 00:04:39,520
Then why not find some exotic matter for us,

59
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:41,470
Hououin-san?

60
00:04:43,390 --> 00:04:48,860
That's all I have to say. But if you have
further objections, I'm listening.

61
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:50,600
Hououin-san!

62
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:55,260
Don't be so damned arrogant,
just because you've some little bit of genius!

63
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:59,720
Wait... She must be an Organization agent.

64
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:59,100
It's hot... It's so hot...

65
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:01,150
The lecture was, itself,

66
00:05:01,150 --> 00:05:04,670
carefully planned
psychological warfare, aimed at me!

67
00:05:04,670 --> 00:05:07,080
Well, I'm not falling for it.

68
00:05:13,370 --> 00:05:16,520
Yanagibayashi
Shrine

69
00:05:15,190 --> 00:05:16,520
Eight...

70
00:05:19,150 --> 00:05:20,500
Nine...

71
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:21,970
Just one more swing.

72
00:05:21,970 --> 00:05:23,100
You can do it!

73
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:24,390
Ten!

74
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:27,320
Way to go, Ruka-kun!

75
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:29,600
Okarin!

76
00:05:30,150 --> 00:05:34,350
O-Okabe-san... No, Kyouma-san.

77
00:05:34,350 --> 00:05:37,340
You forgot the secret words, Rukako.

78
00:05:39,390 --> 00:05:42,520
E-El Psy... Congre...

79
00:05:42,520 --> 00:05:43,780
Congroo!

80
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:45,410
E-Excuse me.

81
00:05:45,410 --> 00:05:48,010
So what did you want me to carry?

82
00:05:48,010 --> 00:05:49,480
Right here.

83
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,740
Thanks.

84
00:05:51,250 --> 00:05:54,850
Mayushii can't carry all this.

85
00:05:54,850 --> 00:05:59,310
My dad got them, and we can't eat them all.

86
00:05:59,310 --> 00:06:00,590
I see.

87
00:06:00,590 --> 00:06:03,250
Thank you for donating these
provisions to the lab.

88
00:06:03,250 --> 00:06:05,510
This will raise lab member morale.

89
00:06:05,510 --> 00:06:08,300
I'm so glad you like them...

90
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:10,520
Um... Well...

91
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:14,100
Ruka-kun practices sword swings daily!

92
00:06:14,100 --> 00:06:19,390
Yes. I promised Oka... I mean, Kyouma-san.

93
00:06:19,390 --> 00:06:24,350
When the Magic Blade Samidare
acknowledges you as a suitable wielder,

94
00:06:24,350 --> 00:06:26,020
it will display its true power.

95
00:06:26,020 --> 00:06:27,010
Do not forget that.

96
00:06:27,010 --> 00:06:27,880
Yes!

97
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:33,810
You got such a deal on it
at the weapons store. Only 980 yen!

98
00:06:33,810 --> 00:06:37,530
Then show me the results of your training.

99
00:06:37,530 --> 00:06:38,970
Can you attempt an exorcism?

100
00:06:38,970 --> 00:06:42,600
I-I suppose... But...

101
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:46,100
If you need a real exorcism,
you should talk to my father...

102
00:06:47,650 --> 00:06:51,650
An evil spirit has possessed my right hand!

103
00:06:51,650 --> 00:06:56,190
Hurry and do the exorcism,
before the power overtakes my entire body!

104
00:06:54,970 --> 00:06:56,190
R-Right!

105
00:06:56,190 --> 00:06:58,880
That's a different hand than last time.

106
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:01,770
The evil spirit possessed
this one today, okay?

107
00:07:01,770 --> 00:07:03,740
<i>Urushibara Ruka.</i>

108
00:07:04,150 --> 00:07:07,060
<i>The mannerisms and voice of a woman...</i>

109
00:07:07,390 --> 00:07:11,060
<i>No... More feminine than any woman.</i>

110
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:12,890
<i>But he's a guy.</i>

111
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:17,770
<i>Taller than Mayuri, but so very thin...</i>

112
00:07:17,850 --> 00:07:19,430
<i>But he's a guy.</i>

113
00:07:19,430 --> 00:07:21,970
<i>Looks great in a Miko outfit...</i>

114
00:07:22,020 --> 00:07:23,930
<i>But he's a guy.</i>

115
00:07:24,730 --> 00:07:26,450
<i>It's already twilight.</i>

116
00:07:26,450 --> 00:07:27,850
<i>And yet, it's so hot.</i>

117
00:07:28,350 --> 00:07:29,970
<i>The cicadas are crying.</i>

118
00:07:30,510 --> 00:07:31,350
<i>But...</i>

119
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,310
<i>He's a guy.</i>

120
00:07:34,310 --> 00:07:36,890
Bye-bye!

121
00:07:39,350 --> 00:07:42,720
Ruka-kun's so great,
able to do those exorcisms!

122
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:44,810
He's a shrine family's son, yes.

123
00:07:48,770 --> 00:07:50,510
Sorry.

124
00:07:52,450 --> 00:07:54,390
Restricted Area
Akihabara Police

125
00:07:54,390 --> 00:07:56,310
It's off-limits?

126
00:07:56,310 --> 00:07:59,850
Yeah, this leads behind the Radio Building.

127
00:08:00,430 --> 00:08:01,590
The Radio Building...

128
00:08:11,210 --> 00:08:12,630
Give me those.

129
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:15,500
You've got work soon, right?

130
00:08:18,610 --> 00:08:19,680
Thank you.

131
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:28,930
I'm working late tonight,
so I'm just going home afterward.

132
00:08:28,930 --> 00:08:30,070
Mayuri...

133
00:08:30,810 --> 00:08:34,250
You really didn't hear a scream, did you?

134
00:08:34,250 --> 00:08:36,420
A scream? When?

135
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:38,220
Today, at the Radio Building.

136
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:41,390
I don't think I did.

137
00:08:42,350 --> 00:08:43,560
I see...

138
00:08:44,220 --> 00:08:45,120
All right.

139
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:46,110
Then that's fine.

140
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:49,020
Oh, Okarin...

141
00:08:50,260 --> 00:08:54,770
So no one remembers...

142
00:08:54,770 --> 00:08:59,180
Not Mayuri. Not Daru. Not Makise Kurisu.

143
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:00,350
Open

144
00:09:00,470 --> 00:09:01,270
Closed

145
00:09:02,290 --> 00:09:05,430
You're closing up early today, Mr. Braun!

146
00:09:05,430 --> 00:09:08,860
I told you not to call me that.

147
00:09:08,860 --> 00:09:11,060
I'm interviewing a part-timer today.

148
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:12,540
A part-timer?

149
00:09:12,540 --> 00:09:15,050
At a dreary shop with no customers,

150
00:09:15,050 --> 00:09:17,520
run by an over-muscled old guy?

151
00:09:17,990 --> 00:09:19,810
You know...

152
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:22,650
'Sup!

153
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:30,120
I heard that's the popular way to say hi now.

154
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:32,130
This can't possibly be your part-timer...

155
00:09:32,130 --> 00:09:33,350
Is that a problem?

156
00:09:33,350 --> 00:09:34,120
Your name?

157
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:35,320
Amane Suzuha.

158
00:09:35,320 --> 00:09:35,880
Age?

159
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:36,680
Eighteen.

160
00:09:36,680 --> 00:09:37,600
Reason for working here?

161
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:38,970
I love CRT TVs!

162
00:09:38,970 --> 00:09:39,560
You're hired!

163
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:41,210
Is this a comedy routine?

164
00:09:41,210 --> 00:09:42,160
Some kind of joke?

165
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:43,520
Who are you?

166
00:09:43,520 --> 00:09:44,990
His name's Okabe.

167
00:09:44,990 --> 00:09:47,430
He's an idiot who rents a room upstairs.

168
00:09:47,430 --> 00:09:49,570
It's not Okabe! It's Hououin—

169
00:09:49,570 --> 00:09:51,620
Shut up! I'll double your rent.

170
00:09:51,620 --> 00:09:52,640
I'm Okabe Rintarou.

171
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:53,520
Hi!

172
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:55,630
Say, what's in those bags?

173
00:09:55,630 --> 00:09:58,850
Special Intelligence Corn
that was donated to the lab.

174
00:09:58,850 --> 00:10:00,890
If you want some, you must
adequately compensate—

175
00:10:00,890 --> 00:10:01,870
Corn?

176
00:10:01,870 --> 00:10:03,530
With the little bumps?

177
00:10:03,530 --> 00:10:05,550
So this is how it looks fresh.

178
00:10:05,550 --> 00:10:06,580
You didn't know?

179
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:07,080
Can I see—

180
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:11,780
The Organization has targeted many people

181
00:10:11,780 --> 00:10:13,570
because they came into contact with me.

182
00:10:13,570 --> 00:10:17,470
Sara, Claudia, Simona...

183
00:10:17,470 --> 00:10:18,900
I see.

184
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:20,740
If you want, we could talk about it.

185
00:10:20,740 --> 00:10:23,960
Don't worry about him.
He's just making that up.

186
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:27,820
Think that if you like.

187
00:10:27,820 --> 00:10:31,660
Someday, the entire world
will bow at my feet.

188
00:10:34,640 --> 00:10:37,780
So, that's what's popular these days...

189
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:57,060
Unknown satellite crashes near
Akihabara Station, around 12:00...

190
00:10:53,790 --> 00:10:56,310
Crashed around 12:00...

191
00:10:57,060 --> 00:10:59,780
So Mayuri and Daru were right.

192
00:11:08,850 --> 00:11:11,100
The conference was canceled?

193
00:11:08,870 --> 00:11:11,100
Doctor Nakabachi Press Conference

194
00:11:11,100 --> 00:11:13,560
Makise Kurisu stabbed...

195
00:11:17,690 --> 00:11:21,870
Was that some kind of hallucination?

196
00:11:27,430 --> 00:11:29,600
@channel

197
00:11:34,570 --> 00:11:36,270
John Titor?

198
00:11:36,290 --> 00:11:39,600
A time traveler's here! LOLOLOL

199
00:11:42,150 --> 00:11:46,680
SERN maintains an exclusive monopoly
on time machines.

200
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:50,610
Neither civilians nor corporations
may acquire one.

201
00:11:50,610 --> 00:11:53,580
They've used the time machine
for their sole benefit,

202
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:56,310
to bring about dystopia.

203
00:11:56,310 --> 00:11:59,890
I've come here to change the future.

204
00:12:00,390 --> 00:12:05,900
To destroy SERN's dystopia,
and to set the world free again.

205
00:12:05,900 --> 00:12:09,390
Then you claim SERN = Dictators?

206
00:12:09,390 --> 00:12:12,020
You mean the so-called
Grandfather Paradox, right?

207
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:12,580
257 Name: Nameless Prophet-san [sage]
All I can think of is the European Laboratory for Particle Physics.

208
00:12:12,020 --> 00:12:13,680
There's no such thing.

209
00:12:12,620 --> 00:12:15,450
451 Name: Nameless Prophet-san [sage]
If you time travel, can you meet yourself in the past?

210
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:16,200
It's possible to meet yourself in the past.

211
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:18,790
If you do, you simply move world lines.

212
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:20,060
What's a world line?
Inb4 parallel worlds.

213
00:12:20,060 --> 00:12:21,750
Let me start by saying

214
00:12:21,750 --> 00:12:25,130
that time isn't a single line,
moving from past to future.

215
00:12:25,130 --> 00:12:31,000
It's comprised of infinite parallel lines,
like rivers, called "world lines."

216
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:35,550
For example, let's say a serial killer
were going to murder you today.

217
00:12:35,550 --> 00:12:38,770
If I came from the future and prevented it,

218
00:12:38,770 --> 00:12:40,750
the world would diverge into two:

219
00:12:40,750 --> 00:12:44,930
a world in which you survived,
and a world in which you died.

220
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:51,220
So, this Titor is Japanese, huh?

221
00:12:51,890 --> 00:12:53,420
A self-proclaimed time traveler,

222
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:56,850
who appeared on the American internet,
in the year 2000.

223
00:12:57,540 --> 00:13:03,100
He claimed he'd come from the year 2036,
to save the future.

224
00:13:03,100 --> 00:13:07,920
He then became famous on the internet,
with several books published about him.

225
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:12,680
I didn't think I'd see some idiot
pretending to be Titor now.

226
00:13:10,660 --> 00:13:12,680
618 Name: Nameless Prophet-san [sage]
Pretending to be? Huh?

227
00:13:13,380 --> 00:13:17,180
Then click this link and go read up on Titor!

228
00:13:18,010 --> 00:13:21,600
Daru must've deleted the link on Titor...

229
00:13:24,830 --> 00:13:26,000
John Titor       About 12 Results

230
00:13:26,020 --> 00:13:27,410
Twelve?

231
00:13:27,410 --> 00:13:28,390
Impossible.

232
00:13:28,390 --> 00:13:32,430
Sure, it was ten years ago, but it was huge!

233
00:13:33,150 --> 00:13:34,520
It can't be!

234
00:13:34,540 --> 00:13:36,330
John Titor       About 56 results

235
00:13:36,350 --> 00:13:37,170
They're not here!

236
00:13:37,170 --> 00:13:39,070
They're not here! What is this?

237
00:13:39,070 --> 00:13:41,350
I had a book collection on him right here.

238
00:13:41,350 --> 00:13:42,370
Damn it!

239
00:13:48,430 --> 00:13:49,300
Hello?

240
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:49,970
Daru?

241
00:13:49,970 --> 00:13:51,050
What is it?

242
00:13:51,050 --> 00:13:52,570
I'm with Feyris-tan...

243
00:13:52,570 --> 00:13:53,680
What happened to the books?

244
00:13:53,680 --> 00:13:54,950
The books?

245
00:13:54,950 --> 00:13:57,200
The books on John Titor.

246
00:13:57,200 --> 00:13:59,570
I had a bunch of them
on the bookshelf, right?

247
00:13:59,570 --> 00:14:00,770
Where'd they go?

248
00:14:00,770 --> 00:14:01,960
Wait, Okarin?

249
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:02,800
What?

250
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:07,810
Who's John Titor?

251
00:14:10,270 --> 00:14:14,470
I stayed up most of the night
looking into John Titor.

252
00:14:14,470 --> 00:14:18,450
I found every bit of information
I could on the internet.

253
00:14:18,450 --> 00:14:19,930
But...

254
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:22,770
I want an answer from Titor.

255
00:14:22,770 --> 00:14:26,780
About ten years ago...
In other words, the year 2000.

256
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:29,460
It's interesting that you should ask that.

257
00:14:29,460 --> 00:14:33,910
But unfortunately,
I've never been to the year 2000.

258
00:14:33,910 --> 00:14:37,270
Nor do I intend to go.

259
00:14:49,970 --> 00:14:51,930
Hey! Wait!

260
00:14:51,930 --> 00:14:55,050
You there! You! You!

261
00:14:55,050 --> 00:14:56,730
You took my picture, didn't you?

262
00:14:56,730 --> 00:15:00,370
You should delete it! For your own sake!

263
00:15:02,530 --> 00:15:03,830
I apologize

264
00:15:03,830 --> 00:15:06,140
if I've made you unhappy.

265
00:15:07,170 --> 00:15:09,260
What were you taking pictures of?

266
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:11,520
Proof.

267
00:15:12,380 --> 00:15:19,810
Of where I walked today...
Of what I saw.

268
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:24,910
I want to ask you about something.

269
00:15:26,930 --> 00:15:28,270
This.

270
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:31,390
That's a really old PC.

271
00:15:31,390 --> 00:15:32,500
Do you recognize it?

272
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:33,680
No.

273
00:15:33,680 --> 00:15:35,140
Do you know anyone who might?

274
00:15:35,140 --> 00:15:37,140
Daru, maybe...

275
00:15:37,140 --> 00:15:38,600
Who is that?

276
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:40,590
Nothing to do with you.

277
00:15:40,590 --> 00:15:42,520
Delete that photo.

278
00:15:44,750 --> 00:15:45,830
Tell me...

279
00:15:45,830 --> 00:15:46,840
The e-mail...

280
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:48,270
For that person.

281
00:15:48,270 --> 00:15:49,930
No!

282
00:15:52,390 --> 00:15:55,360
Are you trying to threaten me?

283
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:56,900
If you tell me,

284
00:15:56,900 --> 00:15:58,180
I'll delete it.

285
00:16:02,270 --> 00:16:03,560
Very well.

286
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:06,330
But I won't sell out my friends!

287
00:16:06,330 --> 00:16:08,850
I'll give you my own address.

288
00:16:10,230 --> 00:16:11,390
What's your name?

289
00:16:11,390 --> 00:16:14,720
It says "Hououin Kyouma" right there!

290
00:16:14,750 --> 00:16:16,680
Oubouin Kyouma

291
00:16:19,030 --> 00:16:20,060
Give me that.

292
00:16:27,090 --> 00:16:28,890
Send me a blank mail.

293
00:16:28,890 --> 00:16:30,660
I'll just send something back.

294
00:16:33,210 --> 00:16:36,430
Welcome back, Master!

295
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:38,890
It's Okarin!

296
00:16:38,890 --> 00:16:42,350
Welcome, Okarin!

297
00:16:42,350 --> 00:16:44,430
Yo, Mayuri.

298
00:16:44,430 --> 00:16:48,340
When I'm working, it's Mayushii Nyan Nyan!

299
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:52,080
Come to think of it,
"Okarin" kinda sounds like "Welcome."

300
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:53,850
Where's Daru?

301
00:16:53,850 --> 00:16:55,390
He's in the back.

302
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:57,390
Kyouma!

303
00:16:57,390 --> 00:16:59,280
I've missed you.

304
00:16:59,280 --> 00:17:02,350
What happened to your promise
to visit every three days?

305
00:17:02,350 --> 00:17:03,370
I'm sorry.

306
00:17:03,370 --> 00:17:05,640
The Organization's sabotage
has been just awful...

307
00:17:05,640 --> 00:17:07,620
The Organization's gone that far?

308
00:17:07,620 --> 00:17:10,410
Then you'll hold another secret meeting
today on defeating them?

309
00:17:10,410 --> 00:17:11,360
That's right.

310
00:17:11,360 --> 00:17:13,430
Give me the usual Stealth Field.

311
00:17:13,430 --> 00:17:14,510
On it!

312
00:17:14,510 --> 00:17:15,890
I wish you'd let me join!

313
00:17:15,890 --> 00:17:16,590
No!

314
00:17:16,590 --> 00:17:19,310
The Organization is far
too vast for you to handle!

315
00:17:19,860 --> 00:17:22,930
But I've got my forbidden special move...

316
00:17:22,930 --> 00:17:23,850
What?

317
00:17:23,850 --> 00:17:26,170
You finally mastered it?

318
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:27,590
That's right.

319
00:17:27,590 --> 00:17:30,180
After months of harsh training
in the Guiana Highlands,

320
00:17:30,180 --> 00:17:33,520
and having overcome
my master's death, at last I...

321
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:36,390
I mastered it!

322
00:17:36,390 --> 00:17:38,390
I'll never forgive you. Ever.

323
00:17:41,640 --> 00:17:43,550
So about what I said in my mail...

324
00:17:43,550 --> 00:17:46,650
I believe talking to a winner
makes me a loser.

325
00:17:47,510 --> 00:17:49,010
Don't worry.

326
00:17:49,010 --> 00:17:51,770
I've no interest in that girl and her lies.

327
00:17:51,770 --> 00:17:54,950
Is this today's "You're the last one
I want to hear that from" thread?

328
00:17:54,950 --> 00:17:57,060
Shut up, cheater!

329
00:17:57,060 --> 00:17:58,550
Your 2D wives are crying.

330
00:17:58,550 --> 00:17:59,970
Feyris-tan is special!

331
00:17:59,970 --> 00:18:02,650
She may be 3D, but she has a 2D soul!

332
00:18:02,650 --> 00:18:04,780
Anyway, look at this.

333
00:18:04,780 --> 00:18:06,590
This picture.

334
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:10,240
That's an IBN 5100, right?

335
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:11,770
IBN?

336
00:18:11,770 --> 00:18:14,270
A legendary retro-PC.

337
00:18:14,270 --> 00:18:16,250
It was about a month ago...

338
00:18:16,250 --> 00:18:19,500
I heard a rumor one was
somewhere in Akihabara.

339
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:20,910
She must've heard that.

340
00:18:20,910 --> 00:18:21,610
What happened?

341
00:18:21,610 --> 00:18:23,300
No one ever found it.

342
00:18:23,300 --> 00:18:26,280
Even the famous "Lightning-Speed
Night Heart" tried to find it and failed.

343
00:18:26,280 --> 00:18:30,210
Meaning it probably never existed
in the first place, is my final answer.

344
00:18:30,210 --> 00:18:32,220
It's that valuable?

345
00:18:32,220 --> 00:18:35,190
It was sold over thirty years ago.

346
00:18:35,190 --> 00:18:39,620
At the time, no one bought PCs.
They were too expensive.

347
00:18:39,620 --> 00:18:41,720
That's how stuff ends up incredibly rare.

348
00:18:45,220 --> 00:18:47,130
That girl...

349
00:18:47,640 --> 00:18:49,770
I sent that mail...

350
00:18:49,770 --> 00:18:51,970
I'm Kiryuu Moeka...

351
00:18:50,930 --> 00:18:57,060
Date/Time:
Sender: The Lightning Shiatsu-ist
Subject: I'm waiting
Hououin-san, I sent that mail!
I'm Kiryuu Moeka!
Age 20! No real job!
I can mail you, right?
I'm sending it,
whether you like it or not!
Moeka

352
00:18:52,460 --> 00:18:57,060
Age 20... No real job...
I'm sending it, whether you like it or not...

353
00:18:57,060 --> 00:19:00,370
This is the same girl I just talked to?

354
00:19:00,370 --> 00:19:01,680
What's wrong?

355
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:05,000
Be glad I didn't sell you out.

356
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,480
It's a rare and valuable PC,

357
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:09,470
but there's a good chance
it's not in Akihabara.

358
00:19:09,470 --> 00:19:12,350
El Psy Congroo.

359
00:19:12,930 --> 00:19:14,640
Master!

360
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:16,170
Here you go nyan-nyan!

361
00:19:16,170 --> 00:19:20,030
It's my "The World's In Danger" omelet!

362
00:19:17,700 --> 00:19:19,220
The World's In Danger!!

363
00:19:20,030 --> 00:19:21,540
Yummy...

364
00:19:21,540 --> 00:19:23,000
Calm down.

365
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:28,350
The World's In Danger!!

366
00:19:30,770 --> 00:19:33,670
Analysis at the university laboratory

367
00:19:30,790 --> 00:19:32,060
Toyko Denki University

368
00:19:33,670 --> 00:19:35,150
reveals that the gel-banas

369
00:19:35,150 --> 00:19:37,220
have been torn apart on a molecular level.

370
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:42,180
So they turned into
something that wasn't a banana.

371
00:19:42,780 --> 00:19:44,200
Isn't that bad?

372
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:46,020
What's going on?

373
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:48,660
Right now, the one thing
that comes to mind

374
00:19:48,660 --> 00:19:52,180
is the EM wave effect from the
Phone Microwave (name subject to change).

375
00:19:52,180 --> 00:19:53,430
Why think that?

376
00:19:53,430 --> 00:19:55,740
My intuition as a mad scientist.

377
00:19:55,740 --> 00:19:57,420
So, no reason.

378
00:19:57,420 --> 00:19:59,510
Okay, it's all set.

379
00:19:59,510 --> 00:20:01,680
Then let's use this.

380
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:11,140
Property of Mayushii

381
00:20:02,430 --> 00:20:05,100
Aren't these Mayushii's?

382
00:20:05,100 --> 00:20:06,020
Don't worry.

383
00:20:06,020 --> 00:20:10,110
I bought them with research funds
Mayuri donated to the lab.

384
00:20:10,110 --> 00:20:11,660
Doesn't that make them hers—

385
00:20:11,660 --> 00:20:14,600
Now, let's toss the whole thing in
and see what happens.

386
00:20:14,600 --> 00:20:16,700
Wouldn't one work? Hurr.

387
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:23,030
Can we really learn the Phone Microwave
(name subject to change)'s true power

388
00:20:23,030 --> 00:20:24,640
that way?

389
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:28,110
That (name subject to change)
is annoying. We should take it off.

390
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:36,970
We can't change the world's ruling structure

391
00:20:36,970 --> 00:20:39,920
if we're stingy with experiment funding!

392
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:42,330
You're the only one who wants to, you know?

393
00:20:42,330 --> 00:20:43,750
Really?

394
00:20:43,750 --> 00:20:45,140
Yeah, of course.

395
00:20:46,580 --> 00:20:47,470
Okay, done.

396
00:20:51,540 --> 00:20:52,270
What's wrong?

397
00:20:52,270 --> 00:20:53,510
It's gone...

398
00:20:53,510 --> 00:20:54,580
The banana's gone!

399
00:20:55,810 --> 00:20:57,270
Impossible!

400
00:20:59,820 --> 00:21:01,070
It's me.

401
00:21:01,070 --> 00:21:02,870
Emergency order 666.

402
00:21:02,870 --> 00:21:04,850
Initiate the cool-off!

403
00:21:04,850 --> 00:21:06,470
Government approval?

404
00:21:06,470 --> 00:21:08,110
No time for that!

405
00:21:08,110 --> 00:21:09,400
Talking to yourself... Fail!

406
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:10,450
Shut up!

407
00:21:10,450 --> 00:21:11,260
Where'd you hide it?

408
00:21:11,260 --> 00:21:14,180
What? You're the one who hid it, Okarin.

409
00:21:15,600 --> 00:21:17,820
I see... I get it!

410
00:21:17,820 --> 00:21:20,410
This must be some kind
of teleporter microwave!

411
00:21:20,410 --> 00:21:22,770
Wh-What?

412
00:21:22,770 --> 00:21:24,660
That's crazy.

413
00:21:24,660 --> 00:21:26,560
Then how do you explain this?

414
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:29,730
We took the banana from the bunch,
put it in the microwave, and...

415
00:21:38,770 --> 00:21:41,600
Gel-bana...

416
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:45,390
But it's completely connected
to the rest of the bunch...

417
00:21:45,390 --> 00:21:48,770
A second ago,
we definitely removed one, right?

418
00:21:48,770 --> 00:21:50,430
I think so...

419
00:21:50,430 --> 00:21:53,410
It's really a teleporter?

420
00:21:53,410 --> 00:21:55,450
Is that what it is?

421
00:21:55,450 --> 00:21:59,770
You're doing an interesting experiment,
Okabe Rintarou.

422
00:21:59,770 --> 00:22:03,340
No, Hououin Kyouma-san, wasn't it?

423
00:22:05,780 --> 00:22:08,880
Makise Kurisu?
